Relevant columns, potential usage, and typical conditions  
----------------------------------------------------------------  
bigquery-public-data.google_dei.dar_non_intersectional_hiring  
• workforce – filter on 'overall' (overall Google work‑force hiring)  
• report_year – filter on 2021  
• race_asian / race_black / race_hispanic_latinx / race_white – racial distribution among 2021 hires  
• gender_us_women / gender_us_men – gender distribution among 2021 hires  

bigquery-public-data.google_dei.dar_non_intersectional_representation  
• workforce – filter on 'overall' (overall Google representation)  
• report_year – filter on 2021  
• race_asian / race_black / race_hispanic_latinx / race_white – racial distribution of 2021 work‑force  
• gender_us_women / gender_us_men – gender distribution of 2021 work‑force  

bigquery-public-data.bls.cpsaat18   (or full_csv‑latest‑data‑is‑2023 – same layout)  
• year – filter on 2021  
• sector / subsector / industry_group / industry – locate NAICS technology industries:  
  – “Internet publishing and broadcasting and web search portals” (NAICS 51913)  
  – “Computer systems design and related services” (NAICS 5415)  
• percent_women – % women; U.S. men share can be derived as 1‑percent_women  
• percent_white / percent_black_or_african_american / percent_asian / percent_hispanic_or_latino – racial distribution in each industry  

Typical conditions  
WHERE workforce = 'overall' AND report_year = 2021  
WHERE year = 2021 AND LOWER(industry) LIKE '%internet publishing%'  
WHERE year = 2021 AND LOWER(industry) LIKE '%computer systems design%'  

Ten exploratory SQL queries (simple → complex)  
------------------------------------------------

```sql
-- 1. Description: List distinct workforce categories available in the  Google hiring table
SELECT DISTINCT `workforce`
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_dei.dar_non_intersectional_hiring`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: Years for which “overall” hiring data exist
SELECT DISTINCT `report_year`
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_dei.dar_non_intersectional_hiring`
WHERE `workforce` = 'overall'
ORDER BY `report_year` DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: 2021 overall hiring – racial and gender shares
SELECT
  race_asian,
  race_black,
  race_hispanic_latinx,
  race_white,
  gender_us_women,
  gender_us_men
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_dei.dar_non_intersectional_hiring`
WHERE workforce = 'overall' AND report_year = 2021
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: 2021 overall workforce representation – racial and gender shares
SELECT
  race_asian,
  race_black,
  race_hispanic_latinx,
  race_white,
  gender_us_women,
  gender_us_men
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_dei.dar_non_intersectional_representation`
WHERE workforce = 'overall' AND report_year = 2021
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Distinct sector names in CPS Table 18 for 2021 (to find technology‐related sectors)
SELECT DISTINCT `sector`
FROM `bigquery-public-data.bls.cpsaat18`
WHERE year = 2021
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Distinct industry_group values under the Information sector, 2021
SELECT DISTINCT `industry_group`
FROM `bigquery-public-data.bls.cpsaat18`
WHERE year = 2021
  AND LOWER(sector) = 'information'
ORDER BY industry_group
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Row for “Internet publishing and broadcasting and web search portals” (NAICS 51913) in 2021
SELECT
  percent_women,
  1 - percent_women AS percent_men,
  percent_white,
  percent_black_or_african_american,
  percent_asian,
  percent_hispanic_or_latino
FROM `bigquery-public-data.bls.cpsaat18`
WHERE year = 2021
  AND LOWER(industry) LIKE '%internet publishing%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Row for “Computer systems design and related services” (NAICS 5415) in 2021
SELECT
  percent_women,
  1 - percent_women AS percent_men,
  percent_white,
  percent_black_or_african_american,
  percent_asian,
  percent_hispanic_or_latino
FROM `bigquery-public-data.bls.cpsaat18`
WHERE year = 2021
  AND LOWER(industry) LIKE '%computer systems design%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Compare gender shares of the two tech industries side‑by‑side
SELECT
  industry,
  percent_women,
  1 - percent_women AS percent_men
FROM `bigquery-public-data.bls.cpsaat18`
WHERE year = 2021
  AND LOWER(industry) IN (
        'internet publishing and broadcasting and web search portals',
        'computer systems design and related services'
  )
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description: UNION ALL – Google overall hiring & representation (2021) versus BLS tech industries
